# The built site.
#
# This repo holds sources — content/, build/ and nothing else that a build can
# regenerate. GitHub Actions builds site/ on every push and publishes it as a
# Pages artifact; see .github/workflows/deploy.yml and the "Publishing" section
# of build/README.md.
#
# The output used to be committed at the repo root. That does not scale: a page
# is 150-230 KB, index.html is a full copy of the current daf rewritten every
# build, and one template change rewrites every page at once. A Shas cycle is
# 2,711 dapim, so committing the output means hundreds of megabytes of history
# for files that are a pure function of content/.
/site/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
